@startuml
!include style.iuml
title Executing a validated recipe addition
autonumber

participant "<u>MishMash</u>" as App
participant "add: AddRecipeCommand" as Add
participant "viewer: RecipeViewer" as Viewer
participant "recipeBook: RecipeBook" as Book

note over App, Add
  The command already holds the validated recipe.
end note
App -> Add : confirmationPrompt(recipeBook)
activate Add
Add --> App : Optional.empty()
deactivate Add
App -> Add : execute(recipeBook)
activate Add
note right of Add : Reject a null recipeBook before formatting.
create Viewer
Add -> Viewer : new RecipeViewer()
activate Viewer
deactivate Viewer
Add -> Viewer : view(recipe)
activate Viewer
note right of Viewer
  Read name, nutrition and ingredients.
  Formatting internals are omitted.
end note
Viewer --> Add : formatted recipe details
deactivate Viewer
note right of Add
  Prepend "New recipe added!"
  to prepare the complete confirmation.
end note
Add -> Book : add(recipe)
activate Book
note right of Book : Append the non-null recipe reference.
Book --> Add : return
deactivate Book
Add --> App : confirmation
deactivate Add
note over App
  executeCommand prints the confirmation.
  readCommands then calls the static method below.
end note
App -> App : <u>displayCommandPrompt()</u>
activate App
App --> App : return
deactivate App

legend bottom
  Solid filled-arrow messages are synchronous calls; dashed messages are returns.
  The default confirmationPrompt implementation is inherited from Command.
  The underlined participant and operation denote static application code.
  The viewer's constructor return and diagnostic logging, including size(), are omitted.
endlegend
@enduml
